```mdl
verdict F-4.2: EchoHost's query executor drops expired feed items from index answers; EDGE's index queries do not.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo-host/src/query/query-executor.ts#QueryExecutor]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo-client-e2e/src/feed-options.test.ts]
  note: |
    The executor computes per-feed cutoffs from stored `maxAge` and filters rows. EDGE's Indexer `queryText` and
    query paths have no `maxAge` filter (searched `indexer/` for maxAge/cutoff), so an expired item stays
    queryable there until the alarm's age trim and the next purge.
```

